               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX/12XX" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1299" calendar="#gregorian">s. xii/xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_598">Witham, Somerset.
                        Charterhouse of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Erased inscription (s.
                        xiv?) at head of first leaf of text: 'Hic liber est ecclesie dei et beate
                        marie de Wytham [. .] / Biblia de dono Walteri quondam prioris de Mertone'.
                        The two lines are probably in the same hand. They are quite invisible by
                        daylight but are retrievable by U. V. (checked 1946 and
                     1963).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Walter, prior of Merton, 1198--1218, became a
                     Carthusian monk in the latter year, according to the annals of Waverley
                     (Annales monastici, ii, p. 290).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Once owned by James Fairhurst of Oldham, and
                     part of his 'Selden collection', it was sold to St Paul's Cathedral in 1949,
                     but then was resold. It was for a while in the ownership of Morgan, Grenfell
                     &amp; Co. of London. It is recorded in MLGB as in the ownership of MR. H. F.
                     Smith of Leicester.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">According to the Schoenberg Database (no.
                     3629), it appeared for auction at Sotheby's on 10 June 1963 (lot 159), and (no.
                     10973) it last appeared for sale at Quaritch in 1992, their catalogue 1151, no.
                     11.</provenance>
               </history>
